-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), regulations 39 and 39.1: EARNINGS IN THE WAITING PERIOD, and
-- WAIVING OF THE WAITING PERIOD FOR APPRENTICES.
-- Written by the piece agent er3 (Sonnet 5.5) on 2026-10-24 from the unofficial plain-text rendering
-- SOR-96-332.txt; nothing here is claimed to be verified against the official text.
--
-- Out of range: ss 19(3)(a), 152.18(3)(a) of the Act (the amount required to be deducted for undeclared or
-- misrepresented earnings, pieces ei1 and ei5), s 25(1)(a) (the Commission's referral to a course, ei2), and the
-- weekly rate of benefits (s 14 of the Act, ei1). Each is an input. The day reg 39.1 came into force is not
-- in the text: an input.

§ `Regulation 39 -- earnings in the waiting period`

-- One amount paid or payable to the claimant in respect of a period in the waiting period, with the facts that
-- decide whether subsection (3) leaves it out.
-- src:696 | (3) For the purpose of calculating the earnings of a claimant during the waiting period, no account shall be taken of amounts paid or payable
-- src:697 | (a) under a wage-loss indemnity plan by reason of illness, injury or quarantine, pregnancy, the care of a child or children referred to in subsection 23(1) or 152.05(1) of the Act or the care or support of a family member referred to in subsection 23.1(2) or 152.06(1) of the Act, of a critically ill child or of a critically ill adult, or under a workers’ compensation plan; or
-- src:698 | (a.1) as an indemnity described in paragraph 35(2)(f); or
-- src:699 | (b) by an employer in respect of sick leave, maternity leave or adoption leave, leave for the care of a child or children referred to in subsection 23(1) or 152.05(1) of the Act or leave for the care or support of a family member referred to in subsection 23.1(2) or 152.06(1) of the Act, of a critically ill child or of a critically ill adult.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 39(3) (src:696-699)
DECLARE `er3 Amount paid or payable in the waiting period` HAS
    amount IS A NUMBER
    `under a wage-loss indemnity plan by reason of illness, injury or quarantine, pregnancy, the care of a child or children referred to in subsection 23(1) or 152.05(1) of the Act or the care or support of a family member referred to in subsection 23.1(2) or 152.06(1) of the Act, of a critically ill child or of a critically ill adult` IS A BOOLEAN
    `under a workers' compensation plan` IS A BOOLEAN
    `as an indemnity described in paragraph 35(2)(f)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `by an employer in respect of sick leave, maternity leave or adoption leave, leave for the care of a child or children referred to in subsection 23(1) or 152.05(1) of the Act or leave for the care or support of a family member referred to in subsection 23.1(2) or 152.06(1) of the Act, of a critically ill child or of a critically ill adult` IS A BOOLEAN

