@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 39(3) (src:696-699)
GIVEN item IS AN `er3 Amount paid or payable in the waiting period`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 39(3) no account is taken of the amount` IF
       item's `under a wage-loss indemnity plan by reason of illness, injury or quarantine, pregnancy, the care of a child or children referred to in subsection 23(1) or 152.05(1) of the Act or the care or support of a family member referred to in subsection 23.1(2) or 152.06(1) of the Act, of a critically ill child or of a critically ill adult`
    OR item's `under a workers' compensation plan`
    OR item's `as an indemnity described in paragraph 35(2)(f)`
    OR item's `by an employer in respect of sick leave, maternity leave or adoption leave, leave for the care of a child or children referred to in subsection 23(1) or 152.05(1) of the Act or leave for the care or support of a family member referred to in subsection 23.1(2) or 152.06(1) of the Act, of a critically ill child or of a critically ill adult`

-- The earnings of the claimant during the waiting period: the amounts paid or payable in respect of periods in
-- it, less those that (3) leaves out.
-- src:696 | (3) For the purpose of calculating the earnings of a claimant during the waiting period, no account shall be taken of amounts paid or payable
-- src:697 | (a) under a wage-loss indemnity plan by reason of illness, injury or quarantine, pregnancy, the care of a child or children referred to in subsection 23(1) or 152.05(1) of the Act or the care or support of a family member referred to in subsection 23.1(2) or 152.06(1) of the Act, of a critically ill child or of a critically ill adult, or under a workers’ compensation plan; or
-- src:698 | (a.1) as an indemnity described in paragraph 35(2)(f); or
-- src:699 | (b) by an employer in respect of sick leave, maternity leave or adoption leave, leave for the care of a child or children referred to in subsection 23(1) or 152.05(1) of the Act or leave for the care or support of a family member referred to in subsection 23.1(2) or 152.06(1) of the Act, of a critically ill child or of a critically ill adult.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 39(3) (src:696-699)
GIVEN items IS A LIST OF `er3 Amount paid or payable in the waiting period`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 39(3) the earnings of the claimant during the waiting period` IS
    sum (map (GIVEN x YIELD x's amount)
             (filter (GIVEN x YIELD NOT (`reg 39(3) no account is taken of the amount` x)) items))

-- (1) The amount deducted is equal to those earnings or, if paragraph 19(3)(a) or 152.18(3)(a) of the Act applies
-- in respect of them, the amount that paragraph requires to be deducted. It is deducted from the benefits
-- payable for the first three weeks for which benefits are otherwise payable.
-- src:694 | 39 (1) If a claimant has earnings in respect of a period that falls in the claimant’s waiting period, an amount equal to those earnings or, if paragraph 19(3)(a) or 152.18(3)(a) of the Act applies in respect of those earnings, the amount required by that paragraph to be deducted, shall be deducted from the benefits payable for the first three weeks for which benefits are otherwise payable.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 39(1) (src:694)
GIVEN earnings IS A NUMBER
      `paragraph 19(3)(a) or 152.18(3)(a) of the Act applies in respect of those earnings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount required by that paragraph to be deducted` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 39(1) the amount to be deducted, before the limit of subsection (2)` IS
    IF `paragraph 19(3)(a) or 152.18(3)(a) of the Act applies in respect of those earnings`
    THEN `the amount required by that paragraph to be deducted`
    ELSE earnings

-- The deduction is made from the benefits payable for the first three weeks (a count of weeks, not a date).
-- src:694 | 39 (1) If a claimant has earnings in respect of a period that falls in the claimant’s waiting period, an amount equal to those earnings or, if paragraph 19(3)(a) or 152.18(3)(a) of the Act applies in respect of those earnings, the amount required by that paragraph to be deducted, shall be deducted from the benefits payable for the first three weeks for which benefits are otherwise payable.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 39(1) (src:694)
DECIDE `reg 39(1) the number of weeks of benefits from which the deduction is made` IS 3

-- (2) The most that can be deducted in respect of the earnings in the waiting period is the rate of weekly
-- benefits.
-- src:695 | (2) The maximum amount to be deducted under subsection (1) in respect of a claimant’s earnings in their waiting period is an amount equal to their rate of weekly benefits.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 39(2) (src:695)
GIVEN `the amount to be deducted under subsection (1)` IS A NUMBER
      `the claimant's rate of weekly benefits` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 39(2) the amount deducted, not above the rate of weekly benefits` IS
    min `the amount to be deducted under subsection (1)` `the claimant's rate of weekly benefits`

-- (1), (2), (3) together: the amount deducted from the benefits of the first three weeks, for the amounts paid or
-- payable in respect of periods in the waiting period.
-- src:694 | 39 (1) If a claimant has earnings in respect of a period that falls in the claimant’s waiting period, an amount equal to those earnings or, if paragraph 19(3)(a) or 152.18(3)(a) of the Act applies in respect of those earnings, the amount required by that paragraph to be deducted, shall be deducted from the benefits payable for the first three weeks for which benefits are otherwise payable.
-- src:695 | (2) The maximum amount to be deducted under subsection (1) in respect of a claimant’s earnings in their waiting period is an amount equal to their rate of weekly benefits.
-- src:696 | (3) For the purpose of calculating the earnings of a claimant during the waiting period, no account shall be taken of amounts paid or payable
-- src:697 | (a) under a wage-loss indemnity plan by reason of illness, injury or quarantine, pregnancy, the care of a child or children referred to in subsection 23(1) or 152.05(1) of the Act or the care or support of a family member referred to in subsection 23.1(2) or 152.06(1) of the Act, of a critically ill child or of a critically ill adult, or under a workers’ compensation plan; or
-- src:698 | (a.1) as an indemnity described in paragraph 35(2)(f); or
